hadiths[37]{hadithnumber,text}:
"4151","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Going out once in the path of Allah, in the morning or in the evening, is better than the world and whatever is in it."""
"4152","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Going out once in the path of Allah, in the morning or in the evening, is better than everything upon which the sun rises and sets."""
"4153","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""One of the prophets went out on a military expedition, and he said to his people: 'None of you should follow me who has married a woman and wishes to consummate the marriage with her but has not yet done so; nor anyone who has built houses but has not yet raised their roofs; nor anyone who has bought sheep or pregnant she-camels and is waiting for them to give birth.' So he went out on the expedition and drew near the town at the time of the Asr prayer, or close to it, and he said to the sun: 'You are under command and I am under command. O Allah, hold it back for us.' So it was held back until Allah granted him victory. Then he gathered the spoils of war, and the fire came to consume them, but it did not consume them. So he said: 'There is misappropriation among you, so let one man from each tribe pledge allegiance to me.' Then a man's hand stuck to his hand. He said: 'The misappropriation is among you, so let your tribe pledge allegiance to me.' Then the hands of two or three men stuck to his hand. He said: 'The misappropriation is among you.' So they brought a large head of gold like the head of a cow and placed it down, and the fire came and consumed it. Then Allah made the spoils of war lawful for us; He saw our weakness and our helplessness, so He made them lawful for us."""
"4154","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""One military expedition at sea is better than ten expeditions on land. Whoever crosses the sea is as though he has crossed all the valleys, and the one who becomes dizzy on it is like one who is rolling in his own blood."""
"4155","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Taking a bath (ghusl) on Friday is obligatory upon every adult."""
"4156","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Trials will cover you like pieces of the dark night. The one most likely to be saved from them will be a man who lives on a high mountain and drinks the milk of his sheep, or a man who holds the reins of his horse beyond the frontiers and eats what he earns by his sword."""
"4157","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Cover your thigh, for the thigh is part of the awrah (what must be covered)."""
"4158","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Cover your thigh, for a man's thigh is part of his awrah (what must be covered)."""
"4159","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Cover the vessels and tie up the waterskins, for in the year there is a night in which a plague descends. It does not pass by an uncovered vessel or an untied waterskin except that some of that plague falls into it."""
"4160","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Cover the vessels, tie up the waterskins, close the doors and put out the lamps, for Satan does not untie a waterskin, nor open a door, nor uncover a vessel. If one of you finds nothing to cover it with except to lay a stick across his vessel and mention the name of Allah, then let him do so, for the little mouse sets the house on fire over its people."""
"4161","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The tribe of Ghifar, Allah has forgiven it; the tribe of Aslam, Allah has granted it safety; and the tribe of Usayyah has disobeyed Allah and His Messenger."""
"4162","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah forgave a man from among those who were before you. He was lenient when he sold, lenient when he bought, and lenient when he demanded repayment."""
"4163","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A prostitute was forgiven. She passed by a dog at the edge of a well, panting, and thirst had nearly killed it. So she took off her leather sock, tied it with her head-covering and drew out some water for it, and she was forgiven because of that."""
"4164","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Hardness of heart and harshness are among the people of the East, and faith and tranquillity are among the people of the Hijaz."""
"4165","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Other than the Dajjal, what is more dangerous for my Ummah than the Dajjal are the misguiding leaders."""
"4166","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It is something other than the Dajjal that I fear most for you. If he emerges while I am among you, I will contend with him on your behalf; and if he emerges while I am not among you, then every man will contend with him on his own behalf, and Allah is my successor over every Muslim. He will be a young man with very curly hair, one of his eyes like a protruding grape. I liken him to Abd al-Uzza bin Qatan. So whoever among you meets him should recite over him the opening verses of Surah al-Kahf. He will emerge from a path between Syria and Iraq, then spread corruption to the right and to the left. O servants of Allah, stand firm!"" The Companions asked: ""O Messenger of Allah, how long will he remain on the earth?"" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Forty days: one day like a year, one day like a month, one day like a week, and the rest of his days like your ordinary days."" The Companions asked: ""O Messenger of Allah, that day which will be like a year, will the prayers of one day be sufficient for us in it?"" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""No; rather, estimate its time and pray accordingly."" The Companions asked: ""How fast will he move through the earth?"" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Like rain driven from behind by the wind. He will come to a people and call them to himself, and they will believe in him and accept what he says. Then he will command the sky and it will send down rain, and the earth and it will produce vegetation. Then their grazing animals will return to them in the evening with their udders longer than ever, full of milk, and their flanks far more stretched. Then he will come to another people and call them, but they will reject what he says, so he will turn away from them, and they will be struck by drought, with nothing of their wealth left in their hands. He will pass by a ruin and say to it: 'Bring out your treasures!' And its treasures will follow him like a swarm of bees. Then he will call a man full of youth, strike him with the sword and cut him into two pieces like the two halves of a target. Then he will call him, and he will come back alive, his face shining and laughing. While he is in this state, Allah will send Isa, son of Maryam. He will descend at the white minaret in the east of Damascus, wearing two yellow garments, with his hands resting on the wings of two angels. When he lowers his head, drops of water will fall from it, and when he raises it, drops like pearls will fall from it. It will not be possible for any disbeliever to catch the scent of his breath without dying, and his breath will reach as far as his sight reaches. Then he will search for the Dajjal until he finds him at the gate of Ludd and kills him. Then there will come to Isa people whom Allah has protected from the Dajjal, and he will wipe their faces and tell them of their ranks in Paradise. While they are in this state, Allah will reveal to Isa: 'I have brought forth servants of Mine whom no one has the power to fight, so take My servants to the Tur.' And Allah will send Ya'juj and Ma'juj (Gog and Magog), and they will swarm down swiftly from every height. The first of them will pass by the Lake of Tiberias and drink all its water, and when the last of them pass by it, they will say: 'There was once water here!' Then they will march on until they reach Jabal al-Khamr, that is, the mountain of Bayt al-Maqdis, and they will say: 'We have killed the people of the earth; come, let us now kill the people of the heavens.' So they will shoot their arrows toward the sky, and Allah will return their arrows to them stained with blood. The Prophet of Allah, Isa, and his companions will be besieged until the head of an ox will be better for one of them than a hundred dinars are for one of you today. Then the Prophet of Allah, Isa, and his companions will humbly implore Allah, and Allah will send upon them a worm in their necks, and by morning they will lie dead as though a single soul had died. Then the Prophet of Allah, Isa, and his companions will come down to the earth, and they will not find on the earth even a hand-span of space that is not filled with the grease and stench of their corpses. So the Prophet of Allah, Isa, and his companions will humbly implore Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, and Allah will send birds with necks as long as those of camels, which will carry the corpses away and throw them wherever Allah wills. Then Allah will send a rain from which no house of clay or of wool will be spared, and it will wash the earth until it leaves it clean like a mirror. Then it will be said to the earth: 'Bring forth your fruit and restore your blessing.' On that day a group of people will eat from a single pomegranate and sit in the shade of its rind, and such blessing will be placed in milk that one milch she-camel will suffice a large group of people, one milch cow will suffice a whole tribe, and one milch sheep will suffice a family. While they are in this state, Allah will send a pleasant wind which will pass beneath their armpits and take the soul of every believer and every Muslim, and only the worst of people will remain, who will fall upon one another openly like donkeys, and it is upon them that the Hour will be established."""
"4167","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Dye your white hair and do not imitate the Jews."""
"4168","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Dye your white hair and do not imitate the Jews and the Christians."""
"4169","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Dye your white hair, but do not bring it near to black."""
"4170","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Dye his head with something, and avoid black."""
"4171","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The one who fights in the path of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, the one who performs Hajj and the one who performs Umrah are the guests of Allah. He called them and they answered His call, and they asked of Him and He gave them."""
"4172","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The one who dies by drowning is a martyr, the one who dies by burning in fire is a martyr, the one who dies of a disease of the stomach is a martyr, the one upon whom a house collapses is a martyr, and the one who is killed defending his own life is a martyr."""
"4173","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The one who drowns in the path of Allah is a martyr."""
"4174","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Fighting is of two kinds. As for the one who fights seeking the pleasure of Allah Almighty, obeys the leader, spends his finest wealth, is gentle with his companion and keeps away from causing corruption in the land, then his sleeping and his waking are all reward. And as for the one who fights out of pride, for show and for reputation, disobeys the leader and spreads corruption in the land, he will not return even with good and bad deeds evenly balanced."""
"4175","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The water for the ritual bath (ghusl) is one sa', and the water for ablution (wudu) is one mudd."""
"4176","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Ghusl is required because of washing the deceased, and ablution (wudu) is required because of carrying him."""
"4177","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Taking a bath (ghusl) on Friday is obligatory upon every adult, and also using the miswak (tooth-stick) and applying whatever perfume one can find, even if it is women's perfume."""
"4178","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Taking a bath (ghusl) on Friday is obligatory upon every adult, and also using the miswak (tooth-stick) and applying perfume if he finds it is obligatory."""
"4179","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The right to the profit goes with the liability."""
"4180","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Sheep and goats are a blessing."""
"4181","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Sheep and goats are a blessing, camels are an honour for their owners, and goodness is tied to the forelocks of horses until the Day of Resurrection."""
"4182","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Sheep and goats are among the animals of Paradise, so wipe away the dirt from their noses and pray in their pens."""
"4183","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The boy whom al-Khidr killed was made a disbeliever from the day he was created, and had he lived, he would have burdened his parents with transgression and disbelief."""
"4184","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A boy is held in pledge for his aqiqah. An animal is slaughtered on his behalf on the seventh day, he is given a name and his head is shaved."""
"4185","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A boy is held in pledge for his aqiqah, so shed blood on his behalf and remove what is harmful from him."""
"4186","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Backbiting is that you mention a man behind his back with a fault that is actually in him."""
"4187","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Backbiting is that you mention your brother with something he dislikes."""
